## Operating / permission modes

Terminal cycles `plan` / `auto-accept` / `normal` via **Shift+Tab** keystroke passed to PTY. Chat has no mode UI — only warnings if non-interactive flag missing.

| Mode                          | Relevancy | Should implement | Note                                                                                                  |
| ----------------------------- | --------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Plan mode                     | 🟢 High   | ✅ Yes            | Read-only investigation phase — strong fit for chat (preview before exec)                             |
| Auto-accept / acceptEdits     | 🟢 High   | ✅ Yes            | Chat needs explicit toggle — currently relies on `--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions` flag w/ no UI |
| Normal mode (per-tool prompt) | 🟢 High   | ✅ Yes            | Tool-call confirm UI — chat lacks interactive prompt path                                             |
| Mode cycle indicator          | 🟢 High   | ✅ Yes            | Pill/badge showing current mode + click-to-cycle (replace Shift+Tab)                                  |
| Shift+Tab cycle shortcut      | 🟡 Med    | Yes              | Keystroke parity w/ terminal — but chat input may swallow Tab                                         |
| bypassPermissions             | 🟡 Med    | 🟡 Maybe         | The task agent flags should be honored                                                                |
| `dontAsk`                     | 🔴 Low    | ❌ No             | Subset of acceptEdits — collapse into auto-accept                                                     |
| `--yolo` (gemini/qwen)        | 🟡 Med    | N                | Map to acceptEdits-equivalent in unified mode UI                                                      |
| `--full-auto` (codex)         | ⚫ N/A     | ❌ No             | Codex = terminal-only provider                                                                        |

## Top priorities

1. **Loop mode** — automated iter w/ pass/fail criteria
2. **Mode UI (plan / auto-accept / normal)** — currently terminal-only via Shift+Tab; chat needs explicit toggle + tool-call confirm flow
3. **Search** — Cmd+F over msg history
4. **Right-click menu** — copy msg/code, reset, clear
5. **Font zoom** — readability
6. **Cmd+Click links** — file paths + URLs
7. **Scroll-to-top/bottom shortcut**
8. **SlayNudge banner**
